Definitions
-----------
Source Code — the human-readable code in this repository.
Binaries — compiled, built, packaged, or otherwise machine-executable forms of the software.
Personal Use — running or testing the software for private, non-commercial purposes.
Educational Use — using the software for teaching, learning, research, or demonstration.
Commercial Use — any use that directly or indirectly generates revenue, supports a revenue-generating activity, or is used to deliver paid services to third parties. Commercial Use includes, but is not limited to: selling the software or derivative works; offering the software as a hosted or managed service (SaaS) with paid tiers; bundling the software into a paid product; using the software to provide services for which customers are charged; or running ads or other monetization tied to the software.
Delivering Services — operating, hosting, or otherwise providing the software (or a derivative) as a service to third parties, whether free or paid, where the operator charges for access, support, hosting, or uses the software to produce billable outcomes.

